# No git writes

The user makes every commit and push themselves. This applies even when a plan,
todo list, or earlier message includes a "commit" or "push" step: skip that step and
tell the user the changes are ready to commit.

Never run:
- `git add`, `git commit`, `git commit --amend`
- `git push` (including deleting remote branches), `git tag`
- `git merge`, `git rebase`, `git reset`, `git revert`, `git cherry-pick`, `git stash`
- `git switch -c` / `git checkout -b` / `git branch -d`
- `gh pr create`, `gh pr merge`, `gh release create`, or any GitHub API call that writes commits or refs

Allowed (read-only): `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git show`, `git blame`,
`git ls-files`, `git fetch`.

If a task truly cannot be finished without a git write (for example, testing a CI
workflow that only runs on push), stop and ask the user first, listing the exact
commands.
